# Real .dockerignore for `docker build -f packaging/rpi5-rak6421/Dockerfile .`
# (build context = repo root). BuildKit — the default in modern docker — honors
# this <Dockerfile>.dockerignore file next to the Dockerfile; legacy builders
# fall back to the repo-root .dockerignore. The root file is a symlink to
# .gitignore, which does not exclude .git (the 80+ MB of context bloat) and
# whose symlink handling is builder-version-dependent — hence this file.
#
# Everything below is verified unnecessary for `pio run -e native`
# (bin/build-native.sh + bin/buildinfo.py read version.properties, not .git).
.git
.pio
release/
venv/
.venv/
.vscode
.idea
.trunk
mcp-server/
*.tar
*.uf2
*.zip
